Z||000003||terryk||09-13-2000||01:01 PM||||The DRAC is the easiest solution on the Fiero ECM. Digital Ratio Adapter Conflabagastinator.<P>What you are thinking.....<P>The problem is that the Fiero VSS drives the speedo and then the ECM, so the correction can't be done in the ECM like the later ones.||||reg||1
Z||000004||elfiero||09-13-2000||01:15 PM||||Ogre,I'm using the 440T4 trans.-4000pulses<BR>per mile.Terryk;VSS output goes to the buffer<BR>first,then tees off to both the speedo and<BR>the ECM.So,the correction must be made B-4<BR>the buffer.The website for the ratio adapter<BR>is;www.atrol.com-check it out,after you remove your foot from your mouth.||||reg||7
Z||000005||terryk||09-13-2000||03:18 PM||||Elfiero,<P>After I remove my foot from my mouth?<P>What is that supposed to mean? <P>Terry<P>This is what I've used until I figure out the other way to do it. Bit cheaper.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.dakotadigital.com/products/interface.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.dakotadigital.com/products/interface.htm</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 09-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||09-13-2000||10:29 PM||||Fiero is 4000ppm off the VSS in any OE transmission. Why you'd read double if the new tranny is also 4000ppm is odd. I don't think gearing would acount for it. Are you using the Fiero VSS or the one that was on the tranny? You could have a wigged out VSS on there. If the new tranny will take Fiero VSS try that.||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||09-13-2000||11:03 PM||||Unless he has one of the newer 4T60's.<P>The ECM and cruise wants 2k. Speedo wants 4k.<P><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 09-13-2000).]||||reg||1
